WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:02.468
-Me choosing not to be
forthright with y'all,

00:00:02.468 --> 00:00:03.837
that was a bad choice.

00:00:03.837 --> 00:00:05.104
But I can't be wasting time

00:00:05.104 --> 00:00:07.306
wishing for a do-over
on all that.

00:00:07.306 --> 00:00:08.807
'Cause that ain't
how choices work.

00:00:08.807 --> 00:00:11.044
No, sir.
No.

00:00:11.044 --> 00:00:14.614
That choice and my
Chicago Bull's starter jacket

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.716
that I let Janelle Rhodes
borrow my sophomore year

00:00:16.716 --> 00:00:18.117
'cause she spilled ketchup
all over herself

00:00:18.117 --> 00:00:19.618
and it looked like
she'd been shot,

00:00:19.618 --> 00:00:22.388
well, those are two things
I ain't ever getting back.

00:00:22.388 --> 00:00:24.290
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
That was the clip

00:00:24.290 --> 00:00:26.158
from the Emmy Award-winning
series, "Ted Lasso."

00:00:26.158 --> 00:00:27.460
We're here with Jason Sudeikis,

00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:32.031
along with co-creators
Brendan Hunt and Joe Kelly.

00:00:32.031 --> 00:00:33.999
[ Laughter ]
Look at that!

00:00:33.999 --> 00:00:36.469
Wow.
Well-rehearsed, gentlemen.

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:38.638
Well-rehearsed.
-Not bad.

00:00:38.638 --> 00:00:42.508
-This is very exciting.
You are now rolling right out

00:00:42.508 --> 00:00:44.210
of season two,
which we're getting to see

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.312
the finale of this week,
into writing season three.

00:00:47.312 --> 00:00:50.583
How's it going so far?

00:00:50.583 --> 00:00:54.253
-I mean --
-What week are we on, four?

00:00:54.253 --> 00:00:55.654
-At least, yeah.
-At least four.

00:00:55.654 --> 00:00:59.125
I mean, the first two weeks were
great because it was the lead-up

00:00:59.125 --> 00:01:02.228
to the Emmys, and then we won
stuff at the Emmys.

00:01:02.228 --> 00:01:04.297
And we really just --
It was a lot of high-fiving.

00:01:04.297 --> 00:01:05.364
[ Both laugh ]

00:01:05.364 --> 00:01:07.667
And now we have
to actually write.

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.602
-Took the next day off.
That cost us a day.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:13.138
-Yep. That's true.
-So we're figuring it out now.

00:01:13.138 --> 00:01:16.109
-Joker --
Right above you, Joker,

00:01:16.109 --> 00:01:19.379
is a -- looks like an idea
for episode 302.

00:01:19.379 --> 00:01:20.546
-Yeah.
-Which one --

00:01:20.546 --> 00:01:23.048
What do you got there?
-"Ted dies"?

00:01:23.048 --> 00:01:27.052
-Yeah, "Ted dies."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:27.052 --> 00:01:29.255
-No wrong answers while
you're blue-skying a season.

00:01:29.255 --> 00:01:32.125
-Blue sky, baby!
-Blue sky -- yeah, exactly.

00:01:32.125 --> 00:01:34.127
Yes, and.

00:01:34.127 --> 00:01:36.663
Brando, this came as no surprise
to me, having known you,

00:01:36.663 --> 00:01:40.833
but you made some very splendid
sartorial choices at the Emmys.

00:01:40.833 --> 00:01:43.970
You were very British early on.

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:46.673
[ Laughter ]
This is a guy right out of --

00:01:46.673 --> 00:01:49.175
-Did not know there
were cameras on, to be fair.

00:01:49.175 --> 00:01:54.814
-So, just to be also
completely honest,

00:01:54.814 --> 00:01:57.483
Jason told me he was gonna
dress as Batman so...

00:01:57.483 --> 00:02:00.486
-Okay.
-I do my Penguin thing.

00:02:00.486 --> 00:02:02.422
You know, we're buddies again,
but hung me out to dry.

00:02:02.422 --> 00:02:04.623
-I said Bruce Wayne.
He heard Batman, for the record.

00:02:04.623 --> 00:02:07.026
-This is --
What I love about this, Brendan,

00:02:07.026 --> 00:02:11.097
is, if you hadn't won, you'd
look like such an ass [bleep]

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:16.936
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.936 --> 00:02:19.638
That was like --
When you went and tried it on,

00:02:19.638 --> 00:02:21.474
you brought a fake Emmy
to see how it'd look.

00:02:21.474 --> 00:02:22.642
[ Laughter ]

00:02:22.642 --> 00:02:25.178
-It's a long walk back
to the parking lot.

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:28.314
-Now, Joe Kelly, this is
the Brendan you met, right?

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:31.217
In Amsterdam, back in the day?
-That was him.

00:02:31.217 --> 00:02:32.785
The pants
are a little looser now.

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:35.288
But that's basically him.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.288 --> 00:02:39.959
-So, we did all meet
in the early 2000s in Amsterdam,

00:02:39.959 --> 00:02:42.228
working for a theater called
Boom Chicago,

00:02:42.228 --> 00:02:45.798
and the conception of this idea
obviously didn't start then,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:48.868
but, like, some of the seeds
were planted, maybe just insofar

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:51.504
as you guys were finding
your way into soccer.

00:02:51.504 --> 00:02:53.339
-Oh, for sure.
Well, I mean, yeah.

00:02:53.339 --> 00:02:55.841
Brendan, you know, fell in love
with the sport over there.

00:02:55.841 --> 00:02:58.344
I mean, safe to say.
-Oh, yeah.

00:02:58.344 --> 00:02:59.545
Hadn't been into soccer at all.

00:02:59.545 --> 00:03:02.481
Then moved to Amsterdam
and caught the bug.

00:03:02.481 --> 00:03:07.187
-And then I -- I only --
I talked a bunch of people

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:08.921
in the theater
to give me 20 guilder

00:03:08.921 --> 00:03:12.224
so I could buy a PlayStation
to play "Tony Hawk: Pro Skater,"

00:03:12.224 --> 00:03:14.193
and then Brendan was like,
"Oh, you should get FIFA 2000,

00:03:14.193 --> 00:03:16.128
as well,"
and then we would play that.

00:03:16.128 --> 00:03:18.731
And Brendan would basically
explain to me the game

00:03:18.731 --> 00:03:21.200
as he's playing Arsenal and
I was playing Manchester United

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.501
and just to sort of
break down the players,

00:03:22.501 --> 00:03:24.103
and it's exactly
the way we ended up doing

00:03:24.103 --> 00:03:26.872
the commercial, like, in 2013,
like, you know, however many --

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:29.208
dang near 12 years later.

00:03:29.208 --> 00:03:31.577
And the way
that Beard and Ted would talk,

00:03:31.577 --> 00:03:34.480
the way he explains
the complications and histories

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:36.549
of the game and how certain
players or certain things,

00:03:36.549 --> 00:03:38.884
that absolutely started
in the greenroom

00:03:38.884 --> 00:03:41.854
or the shiny at Boom Chicago.
-And then you guys were --

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:44.056
Joe, you guys were sort of
sniffing around this idea

00:03:44.056 --> 00:03:46.092
for years, right?
And sort of had it

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.762
in the back pocket,
waiting for the right time?

00:03:49.762 --> 00:03:53.132
-Well, I mean, first,
the NBC promos came up,

00:03:53.132 --> 00:03:55.568
and they kind of
broached the idea with Jason,

00:03:55.568 --> 00:04:00.539
and then it was kind of like,
"Oh, we've got this.

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:03.476
Let's go to London,
and we can do this."

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:06.746
And kind of freaked everyone out
because we refused to hand in

00:04:06.746 --> 00:04:10.883
a script or, like, tell them
about anything we were doing.

00:04:10.883 --> 00:04:13.819
And they're
really, really upset.

00:04:13.819 --> 00:04:15.053
We found all this out
after the fact.

00:04:15.053 --> 00:04:16.088
-Yeah, we didn't know.

00:04:16.088 --> 00:04:17.290
-They didn't say anything
at the time.

00:04:17.290 --> 00:04:19.091
Very polite.
Very lovely people.

00:04:19.091 --> 00:04:20.393
And then, when it was all done,

00:04:20.393 --> 00:04:22.194
they're like "That really --
That was great!

00:04:22.194 --> 00:04:24.930
Like, we were
really freaked out!"

00:04:24.930 --> 00:04:26.432
I was like, "Oh, my God.
We got this."

00:04:26.432 --> 00:04:27.900
We had a great
two days in London,

00:04:27.900 --> 00:04:30.536
went and saw a Tottenham game.
It was great.

00:04:30.536 --> 00:04:33.039
-We're literally
inside our trailer,

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.707
and they're all outside, going,
"What's going on in there?

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.041
Are they writing it?
What's happening?"

00:04:36.041 --> 00:04:37.710
We were playing "Catan."
For hours.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:39.846
-Yeah. Three-person
"Settlers of Catan,"

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.280
which really moves.
You know?

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.449
[ Laughter ]

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.650
That's like --
That's like in paintball.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.519
You know?
-We got to see a skill

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:50.723
that I knew you had, Brendan,
of hula-hooping

00:04:50.723 --> 00:04:53.359
in Coach Beard's big episode.

00:04:53.359 --> 00:04:55.795
Obviously, Joe,
you were aware that Brendan

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.530
had this hula-hooping talent.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.032
Were you worried
that he had maybe --

00:04:59.032 --> 00:05:00.366
that it had degraded
over the years?

00:05:00.366 --> 00:05:04.203
Were you pleased
that he still had it.

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.138
-You're around Brendan,
you walk by his office,

00:05:06.138 --> 00:05:08.407
he's in there hula-hooping
and reading a newspaper.

00:05:08.407 --> 00:05:11.411
So, like, he's kept up with it,
and I respect it.

00:05:11.411 --> 00:05:13.679
-Always warm.
His hips are always warm.

00:05:13.679 --> 00:05:16.249
He's ready to go.
-Did you discover any other

00:05:16.249 --> 00:05:17.750
hidden talents amongst your cast

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:20.519
that you guys
have exploited so far?

00:05:20.519 --> 00:05:24.924
-We -- Billy,
who plays the character Colin,

00:05:24.924 --> 00:05:28.794
is very skilled
and very knowledgeable

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.997
at all of Drake's oeuvre.

00:05:30.997 --> 00:05:33.332
Like, you could give him
like two words,

00:05:33.332 --> 00:05:34.967
and he'll know exactly
what lyric you're doing,

00:05:34.967 --> 00:05:37.736
what song, and then he can
just do it, you know,

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:41.040
in rhythm, like, in time,
and he can do that any point.

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:44.243
And we learned this all because,
last year, during the pandemic,

00:05:44.243 --> 00:05:46.478
the three of us
and then a bunch of fellas

00:05:46.478 --> 00:05:47.980
that play on the game --

00:05:47.980 --> 00:05:49.549
or, play on the team
on the show,

00:05:49.549 --> 00:05:51.984
all played "FIFA" together,
played "Pro Clubs."

00:05:51.984 --> 00:05:54.053
Before the show was even out,
we created AFC Richmond.

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:57.556
We played as our players,
and, yeah, it came out in there

00:05:57.556 --> 00:06:01.560
that old Billy can -- is like
an encyclopedia for Drake,

00:06:01.560 --> 00:06:03.495
Drake songs.
-He's really helpful.

00:06:03.495 --> 00:06:05.198
-He's Drake-opedia.
-He's Drake-opedia.

00:06:05.198 --> 00:06:06.465
-That worked
it's way onto the show,

00:06:06.465 --> 00:06:08.601
and it's a very expensive
15-second scene.

00:06:08.601 --> 00:06:10.836
[ Laughter ]

00:06:10.836 --> 00:06:12.004
-Well, let me tell you, buddy,

00:06:12.004 --> 00:06:14.941
what I wouldn't give
for your music budget.

00:06:14.941 --> 00:06:16.375
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.375 --> 00:06:19.211
-Tell me about it.
-If Wally hums a line

00:06:19.211 --> 00:06:22.081
of something off camera,
we got to shut down for a week.

00:06:22.081 --> 00:06:25.951
[ Laughter ]

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:28.220
You obviously -- You met --
I think we've always --

00:06:28.220 --> 00:06:30.723
whenever we're together,
we talk about the many joys

00:06:30.723 --> 00:06:33.559
and some few shortcomings
of performing

00:06:33.559 --> 00:06:35.327
to the Dutch audiences
we used to do.

00:06:35.327 --> 00:06:38.530
I've been very happy, season 2,
having a Dutch character,

00:06:38.530 --> 00:06:40.899
a Dutch player on the team.
I thought that was very nice

00:06:40.899 --> 00:06:44.570
tip of the cap
to our years in Amsterdam.

00:06:44.570 --> 00:06:46.539
-Yeah, that was --
Write what you know.

00:06:46.539 --> 00:06:47.740
[ Laughter ]

00:06:47.740 --> 00:06:50.709
-Our very, very honest friend,
Saskia Maas...

00:06:50.709 --> 00:06:53.045
-Yes.
-That's who he was named after,

00:06:53.045 --> 00:06:54.981
who gave us all some hard truths
at one time or another.

00:06:54.981 --> 00:06:56.615
[ Laughter ]

00:06:56.615 --> 00:06:58.517
-Yes. She is both the person
that I think

00:06:58.517 --> 00:07:01.287
thinks we're all the funniest
who has also given us

00:07:01.287 --> 00:07:04.089
the most stone-faced looks...
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.089 --> 00:07:06.926
...when we tried doing comedy.
-Gotta earn it.

00:07:06.926 --> 00:07:08.560
You gotta earn --
That's why you know it's real.

00:07:08.560 --> 00:07:12.064
-Yep.
Guys, so nice to see you.

00:07:12.064 --> 00:07:14.566
Congrats. I'm so happy you're
working on season three.

00:07:14.566 --> 00:07:16.435
And thanks
for making time for us today.

00:07:16.435 --> 00:07:17.703
-Thanks, man.
-Thank you.

00:07:17.703 --> 00:07:19.839
-Thank you for having me.
-Love you, guys.

00:07:19.839 --> 00:07:21.374
The season two finale
of "Ted Lasso"

00:07:21.374 --> 00:07:24.710
premieres Friday on Apple TV+,
and Jason Sudeikis will host

00:07:24.710 --> 00:07:28.047
"SNL" with musical guest
Brandy Carlisle October 23rd.

